  "output": {"svg": "architecture.svg", "medium": "documentation and notebook", "alt_text": "An authenticated edge request reaches a bounded orchestrator and tenant-isolated runtime. The model and context can propose but remain untrusted. Every data, effect, and protocol path terminates at a dedicated gateway that enforces workload identity, tenant binding, current policy, evidence, and boundary-specific data or egress controls. A separate highly available identity, policy, and revocation plane produces versioned decisions. Minimized admitted evidence feeds independently operated containment and recovery controls."},
